Subject: [PATCH 10200/11362] Land the two stale-stamp retractions that were
 left stranded

An independent review caught these: two artifacts retracted in the same pass as
commit e0d69d1e30 but neither committed with the 25 nor restored with the 133.
They sat uncommitted in the working tree, one `git checkout` from evaporating,
and they explain the off-by-one between my "26 of 26 carry the retraction note"
and 25 committed files.

Verified before landing, the same checks the batch got: pre-image
flagged_adversarial was True in HEAD for both; both now False with a full
flagged_adversarial_cleared_note; corrigendum_pending preserved in both; and
both pass arc_artifact_lint (exit 0), which is why they were eligible in the
first place and the other 133 were not.

ops/anomaly-escalations.md carries the paper_ready-regression triage lines the
escalator appended for the retracted capstones during that pass. Landed with
them rather than left dangling, since they are the record of what the
retraction triggered.

